+The local tool manifest prepares `hexalith.builds.module.cli` `4.38.1` for the
+Story 6.4 build-preparation candidate. `hexalith-platform.json` accepts versions
+in `[4.38.1, 5.0.0-0)`; older versions are refused with `HXW010` in package mode
+and warned in source mode. The exact release source is
+`16ff70a2321ad576faaac3fe53088c2f1bdacae3` (`v4.38.1`). Its official release
+inventory records successful package, source and control qualification, and its
+NuGet archive identifies that same source. This version is already accepted by
+the Conversations local tool manifest and supplies `prepare-build`.
+
+This is configuration preparation, pending Platform integration qualification.
+The committed Platform Builds gitlink must also identify that exact release
+source; the current committed gitlink does not. An unapplied gitlink patch,
+remote release/feed identities, focused checks and the blocked package retry
+are retained in the Projects Story 6.4 `platform-builds-preparation-20261028`
+evidence receipt. No owner gitlink or consumer identity has been recorded by
+this preparation. Keep the committed-pin tests and all release gates in place.
+
+For package preparation from a consumer workspace, a SemVer tag must identify
+the exact committed Platform revision. Fetching tags cannot qualify an untagged
+revision or a later descendant. The consumer's committed Platform identity,
+staged Builds gitlink, clean Builds checkout and Platform-owned Builds pin must
+agree. Recording a corrected owner tuple, integration qualification and a
+Platform release precede consumer adoption; local candidate checks confer no
+runtime or deployment acceptance.
+
+The [Story 1.13 evidence](_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/evidence/1-13/README.md)
+retains historical acceptance of `4.35.2`. The
